{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p (be aware of numerics).\n    >>> modp(3, 5)\n    3\n    >>> modp(1101, 101)\n    2\n    >>> modp(0, 101)\n    1\n    >>> modp(3, 11)\n    8\n    >>> modp(100, 101)\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper functions for input validation, adhering to design guidance for type and range checks.\n    # These are defined as nested functions to comply with the \"inline helper\" constraint.\n\n    def _ensure_int(value, name):\n        if not isinstance(value, int):\n            raise TypeError(f\"{name} must be an integer.\")\n\n    def _ensure_non_negative(value, name):\n        if value < 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be non-negative.\")\n\n    def _ensure_positive(value, name):\n        if value <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be positive.\")\n\n    # Orchestrate validation calls as specified in the design, type checks before range checks.\n    _ensure_int(n, 'n')\n    _ensure_int(p, 'p')\n    _ensure_non_negative(n, 'n')\n    _ensure_positive(p, 'p')\n\n    # Helper function for modular exponentiation using the iterative \"exponentiation by squaring\" algorithm.\n    # This approach efficiently computes base^exp % mod in O(log exp) time and O(1) auxiliary space.\n    def _modular_exponentiation(base, exp, mod):\n        result = 1\n        base %= mod # Reduce base modulo mod to handle large bases efficiently\n        while exp > 0:\n            if exp % 2 == 1: # If exponent is odd, multiply result by current base\n                result = (result * base) % mod\n            base = (base * base) % mod # Square the base for the next iteration\n            exp //= 2 # Halve the exponent\n        return result\n\n    # Compute 2^n modulo p using the modular exponentiation helper.\n    return _modular_exponentiation(2, n, p)"}
